{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","statement":"The course was taught by Prof. Bernhardt Trout in Fall 2004.","source_span":"Instructor\nProf. Bernhardt Trout\n...As Taught In\nFall\n2004"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","statement":"Lectures meet 2 sessions per week, 1.5 hours per session.","source_span":"Lectures: 2 sessions / week, 1.5 hours / session"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","statement":"The required textbook is Modern Quantum Chemistry: Introduction to Advanced Electronic Structure Theory by Attila Szabo and Neil S. Ostlund, McGraw-Hill, 1989, ISBN 9780070627390.","source_span":"Szabo, Attila, and Neil S. Ostlund. Modern Quantum Chemistry: Introduction to Advanced Electronic Structure Theory. New York: McGraw-Hill, Inc., 1989. ISBN: 9780070627390."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","statement":"Introduction to Quantum Chemistry by Frank Jensen is the recommended text and includes chapter 12, \"Transition State Theory and Statistical Mechanics.\"","source_span":"has a useful chapter, 12 “Transition State Theory and Statistical Mechanics.”"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","statement":"The course uses the software Gaussian03 for quantum mechanical calculations, GaussView as a GUI for job files/visualization, and CPMD (Car-Parrinello Molecular Dynamics).","source_span":"Gaussian03: Used to perform quantum mechanical calculations. GaussView: GUI, used to create job files, run jobs, and visualize output. CPMD: Car-Parrinello Molecular Dynamics Web site."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","statement":"Course hardware includes Sun and Linux machines and the NCSA SGI Origin 2000 with 796 processors.","source_span":"NCSA (National Computational Science Alliance): SGI Origin 2000 (796 processors)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","statement":"The course has five problem sets and requires each student to complete a final project.","source_span":"There are five problem sets in this course. Each student is required to complete a final project."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","statement":"Grading is Homework 30%, Participation 20%, Final Project 50%.","source_span":"Homework\n30%\nParticipation\n20%\nFinal Project\n50%"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","statement":"There are no specific prerequisites for the course, only permission of the instructor.","source_span":"There are no specific prerequisites, just permission of the instructor."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","fact_refs":[0],"question":"Who taught MIT's 10.675J Computational Quantum Mechanics of Molecular and Extended Systems, and in what term?","answer":"Prof. Bernhardt Trout taught it, as offered in Fall 2004."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What is the required textbook for 10.675J, and who are its authors?","answer":"The required textbook is \"Modern Quantum Chemistry: Introduction to Advanced Electronic Structure Theory\" by Attila Szabo and Neil S. Ostlund (McGraw-Hill, 1989, ISBN 9780070627390)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","fact_refs":[7],"question":"How is the final grade for 10.675J broken down?","answer":"Homework counts for 30%, participation for 20%, and the final project for 50%."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","fact_refs":[6],"question":"How many problem sets does 10.675J have, and is a final project required?","answer":"There are five problem sets, and each student is required to complete a final project."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What hardware does the 10.675J course mention for quantum calculations, and how many processors does the NCSA machine have?","answer":"The course mentions Sun and Linux machines plus the NCSA SGI Origin 2000, which has 796 processors."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What software packages are used in 10.675J?","answer":"Gaussian03 is used to perform quantum mechanical calculations, GaussView is a GUI for creating job files and visualizing output, and CPMD is used for Car-Parrinello Molecular Dynamics."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_10-675j-computational-quantum-mechanics-_syllabus","fact_refs":[8],"question":"Are there specific prerequisites required to take 10.675J?","answer":"No, there are no specific prerequisites — only permission of the instructor is required."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_assignments","statement":"The course was taught by Prof. Charles Caldart and Prof. Nicholas Ashford in Spring 2006.","source_span":"Instructors\nProf. Charles Caldart\nProf. Nicholas Ashford\n...As Taught In\nSpring\n2006"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_assignments","statement":"The writing assignment is due at Session #12.","source_span":"Writing Assignment\nDue: Ses #12"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_assignments","statement":"The writing assignment asks students to prepare an approximately 5-page memo outlining a coordinated federal strategy for using existing statutes to reduce indoor exposure to toxic substances.","source_span":"prepare a short memo (approximately 5 pages) outlining a coordinated federal strategy for using existing statutes (as provided in the materials for this course) to reduce indoor exposure to toxic substances"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_assignments","statement":"For the assignment, \"indoor\" exposures are defined as all indoor exposures except those in manufacturing workplaces.","source_span":"“Indoor” exposures, for this purpose, are defined as all indoor exposures except those in manufacturing workplaces."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_assignments","statement":"Students must indicate what they think the basic health-perspective problems are and how their strategy addresses those problems, prioritizing more pressing or more regulable issues.","source_span":"Your paper should indicate what you think the basic problems are (from a health perspective), and how you believe your strategy addresses those problems... you will want to prioritize, and to focus your strategy on those which either are more pressing, are more amenable to regulation, or both."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_assignments","fact_refs":[0],"question":"Who taught Technology, Law, and the Working Environment (10.805J), and when was it offered?","answer":"It was taught by Prof. Charles Caldart and Prof. Nicholas Ashford, offered in Spring 2006."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_assignments","fact_refs":[1],"question":"When is the writing assignment due in 10.805J?","answer":"The writing assignment is due at Session #12."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_assignments","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What is the topic and approximate length of the writing assignment in 10.805J?","answer":"Students write a roughly 5-page memo outlining a coordinated federal strategy for using existing statutes to reduce indoor exposure to toxic substances."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_assignments","fact_refs":[3],"question":"Which indoor exposures are excluded from the scope of the 10.805J writing assignment?","answer":"Exposures occurring in manufacturing workplaces are excluded from the definition of \"indoor\" exposures for this assignment."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_assignments","fact_refs":[4],"question":"Besides proposing a strategy, what else must students address in the 10.805J writing assignment?","answer":"They must state what they think the basic health-perspective problems are, explain how their strategy addresses those problems, and prioritize the issues that are most pressing or most amenable to regulation."}
